      (Secondary)"
    description: Mathematical Subject Classification
abstract: "We demonstrate that the odd values ζ(2k+1) of the Riemann zeta
  function are structurally determined by φ=(1+√5)/2 and π. The Euler product of
  ζ is built from local factors f_p(s), one for each prime. We prove that the
  Frobenius lift at each prime p≠5, congruent modulo p to φ^p = F_p φ +
  F_{p-1}—where F_n is the n-th Fibonacci number—determines the splitting type
  of p in Z[φ], and hence, with the ramified prime 5, which admits no lift,
  every f_p(s). These lifts constitute 𝔽₁-descent data in the sense of Borger
  away from 5. Through the Dedekind factorisation ζ(s) = ζ_ℚ(√5)(s)/L(s,χ_5),
  this determines ζ(s) completely: the Frobenius structure implies the Euler
  product at every level (primes, splitting types, local factors, L-function),
  each implication proved, anchored by the base case L(1,χ_5) = 2logφ/√5 (the
  class-number formula for ℚ(√5)), which expresses the L-function value entirely
  in terms of φ; and the factorisation is a natural isomorphism over ℚ and the
  quadratic fields of discriminant dividing 20. The determination fixes the odd
  values through the pentagonal arithmetic without evaluating them, and by
  itself it does not decide their arithmetic nature. The arithmetic is
  formalised in Lean 4 with Mathlib, and every statement marks the evidence it
  rests on."
